# AiDashVideo .gitignore
#
# Conventions this file assumes (keep them when implementing later milestones):
#   .local/            one ignored root for everything operator-local: acquired model weights and
#                      their upstream LICENSE files (.local/models/), upstream clones and out-of-tree
#                      native builds (.local/src/, .local/native/), runtime state when running from
#                      a checkout (.local/var/: db, cas, staging, outbox, run, log, projects),
#                      generated fixtures and annotations (.local/fixtures/), scratch output of melt /
#                      ffmpeg / sam3 / whisper runs (.local/scratch/), remote-adapter credentials
#                      (.local/credentials/), redirected HOME/XDG/HF/TORCH caches (.local/home/),
#                      and the operator-controlled evidence store (.local/evidence/).
#   docs/evidence/     committed milestone reports and small text/JSON manifests only. Media, frames,
#                      overlays and other binaries referenced by a report live in the local evidence
#                      store; a "raw/" subdirectory or a "local" symlink there is always ignored.
#   docs/implementation/  private operator briefs, deliberately never published.
#
# Editing rules: never add a global rule for *.lock (uv.lock), *.json, *.jsonl, *.xml, *.sql, *.ts,
# *.png, *.svg, *.csv, *.txt, *.md, *.srt or *.vtt, and never ignore .python-version. APFS folds
# case, so a rule such as "core" or "Testing/" would hide a same-named package here but not on Linux;
# anchor or suffix such rules. Re-include with "!" directly below the rule it relaxes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Local-only roots and root-level staging guards
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.local/
/docs/implementation/
# handover staging written by scripts/make_handover_archive.sh; the archive itself lands outside the repo
/handover/
# local Claude helper binary that must never be committed
/claude-hfi
/docs/evidence/**/raw/
/docs/evidence/local
/tests/fixtures/generated/
.aidashvideo/
/var/
/tmp/
/scratch/
/models/
/checkpoints/
/weights/
/fixtures/
# upstream clones cloned at the repo root instead of .local/src/
/whisper.cpp/
/sam3.cpp/
/mlt/
/ffmpeg/
/third_party/**/build/
/vendor/**/build/
# stray outputs tools drop into the current directory when run from the repo root
/*.png
/*.patch
/*.diff
/junit*.xml
/profile.*
nohup.out

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Python toolchain: uv, bytecode, pytest, Ruff, type checkers, coverage, packaging, profilers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.venv*/
/.uv-cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
.hypothesis/
.benchmarks/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
/coverage.xml
/coverage.json
/coverage.lcov
*.py,cover
/dist/
/build/
*.egg-info/
*.whl
*.prof
*.pstats
*.lprof
memray-*
*.speedscope.json
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Native builds: whisper.cpp, sam3.cpp, MLT or binding builds (CMake / Ninja / Xcode / Metal / CoreML)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cmake-build-*/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
CMakeLists.txt.user*
/Testing/
_deps/
build.ninja
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.o.d
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.pch
*.air
*.metallib
*.dSYM/
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
.ccache/
.sccache/

